Description:

The MANAGED-ID parameter is now stripped from ATTACH properties of iTIP
messages that arrive over iMIP.  A MANAGED-ID is meaningful only on the
server that issued it (RFC 8607, Section 4.3).  Previously a sender who knew
the content of a recipient's managed attachment could send an invitation
carrying that attachment's MANAGED-ID; when the recipient deleted the
unwanted event, the attachment's reference count was decremented and the
attachment could be expunged from the legitimate event that owned it.
Servers with :imapdconf:`caldav_allowattach` disabled were not affected.


